far cry 6 is set to take us to the  fictional island of yara to face  dictator anton castillo and his  oppressive regime and while it sticks  pretty closely to the far cry formula in  many ways there's still a lot of new  stuff to dig into here's everything you  need to know about far cry 6. for more  make sure to like this video and  subscribe  set in the present day far cry 6 occurs  in a time of great political turmoil  within yara as a country frozen in time  due to economic sanctions and  isolationism the population begins to  rise up against castillo's oppressive  regime  which has run on his ambition to rebuild  the country to its former glory when  yara becomes paradise  my methods  no one will care you'll play as danny  rojas a native yaran who was caught up  in the uprising to overthrow castillo  and free yara from the presidente's  control teaming up with a guerrilla  faction you'll explore urban and rural  areas of the island confronting  castillo's army and engaging in the  familiar open-world antics you'd expect  in a far cry game how was my day well i  followed a bloodthirsty rooster into  combat after he blew up a truck  another change coming to far cry 6 is  the return of the voiced protagonist who  will be present in cutscenes and have  more agency in the story than most other  far cry lead characters unlike many  other far cry protagonists who are often  outsiders making their way through a  foreign land dany has deep ties to the  island making their investment in its  future more personal you'll be able to  choose between a male or female dany and  far cry 6 will also feature moments  where the game transitions to a third  person perspective those moments won't  just be limited to cutscenes either  you'll see that pov shift when you use  your supremo backpack and when dany  enters friendly gorilla camps  ubisoft has described yara as its most  ambitious open world yet and it includes  a mix of jungles coastal towns farmland  and urban environments to explore the  latter of which is a rarity for the  series throughout the game you'll  acquire weapons gadgets and vintage  vehicles based on technology handed down  and recycled from decades past if all  that sounds like too much to handle by  yourself don't worry you can play in  co-op after completing the early game  mission do or die by and large far cry 6  doesn't deviate much from the loop and  gameplay experience of recent far cry  games this loop focuses heavily on  exploring your surroundings engaging  inside missions retaking outposts and  eliminating key members of castillo's  military to destabilize their control of  the island nation it's familiar and  still looks to capture those same  thrilling moments of open world hijinks  that you would expect from the series  however far cry 6 presents a bit more  flexibility with how you go about facing  off against castillo's regime one of the  more significant innovations in far cry  6 is the new weapon types which now  include three special categories of  firearms and gear the first type is the  regular variety which includes standard  pistols assault rifles and shotguns a  mix of recycled equipment passed down  from the cold war era along with modern  weapons stolen from castillo's army the  second type is known as the resolver  improvised weapons made up of junk items  and scrap along with the minigun there's  also a flamethrower and a disc launcher  that fires burned cd copies of the 90s  hit song the macarena  the final weapon type is supremos  specialized augmented backpacks that can  unleash super moves such as a back  mounted mortar launcher or rocket  powered jetpack furthermore all of these  weapons are customizable letting you  turn a simple handgun into a machine  pistol with a drum magazine complete  with a nice paint job and charm there  are also different ammo types that can  hit enemy weaknesses and take them down  much more easily player and loadout  customization has a deeper role in this  game than in earlier entries along with  the weapon augments you can also  customize your repurposed classic muscle  or town cars with different decals and  guns and even deck out dany with varying  options of clothing that offer bonus  perks such as increased stealth and  better weapons handling you can also  change the appearance of your gear and  keep its stats if you want to stealth is  much more viable as well you can even  holster your gun to hide in plain sight  and bribe roaming guards to avoid  engagements  christmas trees do you even grow those  here mexicans pay crazy money for this  how you think the president defunded  maria's new face  [Music]  returning from far cry 5 is the renamed  fangs for hire feature now it's called  amigos which allows you to partner up  with allies met in the main story one of  which is a crocodile named guapo while  all the amigos will be animals world  director benjamin hall confirmed that  the human element of the yara  insurrection would come from like-minded  people that will join the fight other  animals in the game can be hunted for  meat to trade and horses can get you  from a to b in a gif there's gonna be  plenty of dlc for far cry 6 coming over  the next few months in terms of free  content there'll be crossover missions  featuring rambo danny trejo and even  stranger things that you can play either  solo or in co-op there'll also be weekly  insurgencies that involve you tracking  down castillo's underlings to earn new  gear there's also going to be special  operations which take you to unique new  areas of yara and will introduce new  gameplay mechanics as you snatch highly  unstable chemical weapons from anton's  arms dealers and gets the extraction  point before it overheats if you buy the  season pass you can play as villains  from previous games including vas pagan  min and joseph seed to better understand  those characters you'll also receive a  copy of far cry blood dragon and weapons  armor vehicles and a new fang for hire  so there we have it everything you need  to know about far cry 6 before you delve  in for more on the game subscribe or  head over to gamespot.com where you can  also learn more about ubisoft's  employees taking action to change  hostile company culture and how the  company itself has responded i'm on  twitter at lucy james games and i'll see  you next time  you
 

